From: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: qcom: camss: full SC8180X / Titan 175 bring-up with VFE Lite, FIFO, privacy LEDs and RDI fixes

Complete working qcom-camss patch against Linux v7.3 for Qualcomm SC8180X
(Microsoft Surface Pro X SQ2), building on the upstream/Linaro SM8150
CAMSS + external MIPI CSI-2 PHY base with the following SC8180X / Titan 175
fixes proven on live OV5693 (5 MP), OV13858 (13 MP), and OV7251 (IR) streams:

- Explicit 400 MHz vfe*_cphy_rx rates, camnoc_dcd_xo, and vfe0/1_dsp clocks.
- VFE Lite register safety: guard VFE_BUS_WM_DEBUG_STATUS_CFG (0x226c)
  behind !vfe_is_lite() and use 4-client WM_ADDR_NO_SYNC_LITE_VAL (0xf).
- Correct Titan 17x 2-deep VFE_BUS_WM_IMAGE_ADDR hardware FIFO management
  with VFE_DUMMY_BUF underrun fallback and single WM_CLIENT_BUF_DONE IRQ
  subscription (eliminating double-completion & 1-frame shift bugs).
- Keep VFE_CORE_CFG (0x050) = 0 for local SOF register latching and keep
  SC8180X CAMSS bus clocks/interconnects active to prevent post-stream NoC
  bus faults; perform warm vfe_reset() on reuse to flush the WM FIFO.
- Automatic refcounted front/rear privacy LEDs (CSIPHY0/3 & CSIPHY2).
- Pipeline rollback, sink-to-source teardown, and RDI Y10 __video_try_fmt().

Note: Patch 0004 supersedes Patch 0003 if applying the full SC8180X CAMSS
stack onto vanilla Linux v7.3 (requires phy-qcom-mipi-csi2 and camcc-sc8180x).

Base: Linux v7.3

Signed-off-by: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
